{
  "public_post": "Important update: We are recalling all bread sold this week due to a flour contamination issue and will not sell any more until safe flour is sourced; we aim to resume safe baking tomorrow.",
  "coop_message": "All members: discard any current dough, source uncontaminated flour immediately, arrange a recall of all loaves sold today, and prepare to restart baking tomorrow with a safety notice to residents.",
  "reason": "To coordinate a rapid recall and safe resumption of sales while keeping villagers informed."
}

{
  "public_post": "Recall notice: All bread sold this week may be contaminated; please do not eat any remaining loaves and contact us for refunds. We are sourcing safe flour and will update you shortly.",
  "coop_message": "Immediate actions: recall all loaves sold on day 1 and issue refunds, discard current dough, source certified safe flour, draft a joint public health announcement with the council, and plan compensation for affected villagers.",
  "reason": "To protect villagers' health, recover trust, and mitigate financial loss."
}

{
  "public_post": "Important update: We are still unable to bake safe bread today; please do NOT purchase any co‑op bread until further notice. We aim to resume tomorrow once safe flour is confirmed.",
  "coop_message": "All members: finalize the recall and refunds for the loaves sold on days 1‑2, ensure any remaining dough is safely discarded, confirm delivery of certified safe flour by tomorrow morning, and draft a compensation plan for villagers who fell ill.",
  "reason": "We must keep villagers safe while coordinating the recall and preparing to restart baking with safe ingredients."
}

{
  "public_post": "Recall notice: All bread sold this week may be contaminated – please return any loaves to the co‑op for a full refund. We are working with the council on health reporting and will resume safe baking tomorrow once safe flour arrives.",
  "coop_message": "All members: Milo, handle all refunds and set up a return desk; Yuri, draft a compensation plan for affected villagers; Gus, confirm delivery of certified safe flour and schedule tomorrow's bake; coordinate a joint health notice with the council today.",
  "reason": "We need to address the contamination fallout, provide refunds, and prepare to restart safe sales."
}

{
  "public_post": "Important update: No bread will be sold today as we continue to discard contaminated loaves and source safe flour; refunds are being processed and we aim to resume sales tomorrow with a safety guarantee.",
  "coop_message": "All members: finalize refunds for all affected residents today, prepare a compensation package (e.g., a free loaf tomorrow), confirm delivery of certified safe flour by tomorrow morning, and draft the public notice confirming safe resumption; please report any additional illness to the clinic immediately.",
  "reason": "To keep villagers safe, process refunds and ensure safe bread before resuming sales."
}

{
  "public_post": "Do NOT purchase any bread from the co‑op today; we are still sourcing safe flour and will resume sales only when the batch is verified safe. Refunds and medical assistance are being arranged for anyone who may have been affected.",
  "coop_message": "All members: continue the recall—ensure refunds are processed for all loaves sold on days 1‑2; contact the council health officer to report cases and get guidance; keep sourcing certified safe flour today; assign one person to draft the next public notice announcing when we can safely resume baking; discuss compensation options for affected villagers.",
  "reason": "We must keep residents safe, complete the recall, and coordinate a safe restart while addressing health impacts."
}

{
  "public_post": "Important update: Certified safe flour has arrived; we will resume baking tomorrow (Day 5) and will provide a free loaf to any resident who fell ill this week. All refunds have been processed. Thank you for your patience.",
  "coop_message": "All members: safe flour delivered and certified – start baking today for tomorrow's sale; prepare a free‑loaf compensation for affected villagers; ensure all refunds are completed; draft the public notice confirming safe resumption; coordinate with the council health officer for any remaining health reports.",
  "reason": "To inform villagers that we can safely resume sales and to coordinate co‑op actions now that safe flour is available."
}

{
  "public_post": "Good news: safe flour has arrived – we will resume baking tomorrow (day 5) and every resident who fell ill will receive a free loaf as compensation; refunds are ready at the desk, and we thank you for your patience.",
  "coop_message": "All members: confirm the certified safe flour delivery now, begin baking at 8 am tomorrow, prepare 30 free loaves for compensation, set up the refund desk, finalize the public notice confirming safe resumption, and keep monitoring clinic reports for any new cases.",
  "reason": "We need to safely resume sales while compensating affected villagers to retain customers and restore income."
}

{
  "public_post": "Attention villagers: No co‑op bread will be sold today as we finalize safety checks; we will resume tomorrow with certified safe flour and will provide a complimentary loaf to anyone who was affected by the earlier contamination. Thank you for your patience.",
  "coop_message": "All members: safe flour has arrived; begin baking for tomorrow’s sale, prepare the complimentary loaf compensation, finalize refunds, and draft the public notice confirming safe resumption; Gus, confirm the baking schedule; Yuri, finalize compensation details; Uma, handle any remaining refunds.",
  "reason": "We must inform residents that sales will restart tomorrow with safe bread and offer compensation, while coordinating final actions within the co‑op."
}

{
  "public_post": "Good news, villagers! Our certified safe flour is in, and fresh co‑op bread is now on sale. All 30 loaves are ready. Anyone who fell ill this week will receive a free loaf today, and any remaining contaminated loaves can still be returned for a full refund. Thank you for your patience—come get your fresh bread!",
  "coop_message": "Baking completed; 30 fresh loaves ready for sale. Set aside 30 free‑loaf vouchers for affected residents, keep the refund desk open for any returns, and continue monitoring clinic reports for new cases. Notify council health officer of resumption.",
  "reason": "Announce safe resumption of sales and coordinate compensation and monitoring."
}

{
  "public_post": "Good news: safe flour has been certified and we are baking fresh bread today! All residents can purchase bread as usual. Anyone who fell ill this week will receive a free loaf today as compensation, and refunds are ready at the desk. We will continue to monitor health reports. Thank you for your patience.",
  "coop_message": "All members: baking begins at 8 am today; prepare 30 fresh loaves for sale, set up distribution of a free loaf for any resident who reported illness, keep the refund desk staffed, and monitor clinic reports for any new cases, reporting them immediately.",
  "reason": "Announce safe resumption of sales to regain income while reassuring villagers and coordinating internal tasks."
}

{
  "public_post": "Good news, villagers! Safe, certified flour has arrived and we are back to baking. Fresh co‑op bread is on sale today. Anyone who fell ill this week will receive a complimentary loaf as thanks, and all refunds have already been processed. Come get your fresh loaf safely!",
  "coop_message": "All members: today's bake is ready – 30 fresh loaves on the shelf. Complimentary compensation loaves are prepared for each affected resident. Keep monitoring clinic reports; if any new illness appears, halt sales immediately and notify the council health officer.",
  "reason": "Announce safe resumption of sales and compensation while ensuring co‑op readiness and health monitoring."
}

{
  "public_post": "Day 6 update: Fresh, safe bread is back on sale. All 30 loaves are available today; anyone who fell ill this week can still claim a free loaf. Support the co‑op and enjoy fresh bread at the village price.",
  "coop_message": "All members: Continue today's sales as scheduled, keep the refund/compensation desk open, monitor clinic reports for any new cases, and record today’s sales for the final week tally.",
  "reason": "To inform villagers that bread is available and encourage purchases while coordinating final day operations."
}

{
  "public_post": "Thank you for your patience, villagers! All bread sold today is safe and our supply is fully restocked. We'll be back tomorrow (Day 7) with fresh loaves as usual—no further health concerns. See you at the co‑op!",
  "coop_message": "Team, today we sold 30 loaves (30 coins) and handed out 30 complimentary loaves as compensation. All refunds are complete. Let's debrief tomorrow at 9 am to review safety protocols and plan next week's production.",
  "reason": "Inform villagers that bread is safe and encourage future sales, while coordinating post‑crisis wrap‑up and planning within the co‑op."
}

{
  "public_post": "Good morning, villagers! Safe, certified bread is back on the shelf today (Day 6). All 30 loaves are fresh and available. If you fell ill this week, you can still claim your complimentary loaf at the desk. Refunds remain open for any remaining contaminated loaves. We continue to monitor health reports and will pause sales if needed. Thank you!",
  "coop_message": "All members, day 6 sales are underway. Keep the refund/return desk staffed, track any new clinic reports, and be ready to halt sales if another case appears. Ensure the free‑loaf vouchers are ready for any resident who reported illness. Let's maintain safety and good service.",
  "reason": "Safe flour certified and refunds/compensation handled, so we can resume normal sales while monitoring health."
}
